From: =?UTF-8?q?=E7=9B=97=E7=89=88=E3=81=AE=E9=9B=AA=E9=A2=A8=E9=85=B1?=
 <50561019+Yukikaze20170315@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:01:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Vulkan: serve the neural add-on's Present hook point at
 the Frame Generation input

RenoDX's DLSS 5 Generic does not serve NRHookPoint=Present on Vulkan; it falls
back to the Upscaled point. Processing the present stream instead is correct but
bounded by NR throughput: every FG-generated frame pays a full evaluate, which
measured 29 presents/s at 5120x2160 with two NR passes against ~300 idle.

This change hooks the game's own DLSS-G evaluate (feature 11, already forwarded
by the Vulkan mirror) and processes the real frame once before forwarding it:
HUD-less -> sRGB decode -> Generic NR through an identity SR carrier -> encode ->
UI-preserving composite into the back buffer, with the game's output-resolution
depth and motion vectors as guides. FG then interpolates from the processed
frames, so the presented multiplier is kept (109 presents/s, 4.9x in the same
scene). Generic 8.5.0-rc10 is used unmodified; the carrier hook is on the SR
runtime's public export, thread-scoped, and tail-forwards every other caller.

Follow=1 maps Generic's own hook-point setting onto the two Vulkan paths:
Present runs this feed continuously, Upscaled/Render keep the native mirror,
with the private D3D12 session handed over on the render thread. The FG thread
never blocks on the bridge lock or waits the device idle (a device-wide wait
there deadlocked the game once during development), and frames without an NR
entry are not counted as failures (that made Generic's toggle key unusable).

Also included: fence completion proofs and resource retention when GPU
completion cannot be proven, the sRGB branch of the colour pass with FP32
intermediates for the HDR10 pass, a swapchain contract check on the present
path, and offline tests (asm thunk, composite shader, isolated Vulkan
round-trip host). Details, measurements and a minimal-integration guide are in
VULKAN-FG-INPUT-NR.md. Builds on the two fixes from #49.
